<title>FRANCE: French express train derails, five injured.</title>
<headline>French express train derails, five injured.</headline>
<dateline>LILLE 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A regional express train powered off the tracks after rocks fell into its path in northern France on Friday but only five people were slightly injured, the SNCF state railways said.</p>
<p>The train, made up of four carriages and carrying 35 passengers, was travelling at 90 kph (55 mph) and stayed upright when it left the rails at the town of Saint-Hilaire-sur-Helpe near the city of Lille.</p>
</text>
